          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Why these, in this order",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1 Rio: the largest pool of late orders that one carrier conversation can fix; it is late even on local deliveries (page 3). 2 Northeast: 19-25 day lead times and 12-22% late rates are a network and promise problem, so promises and partners are set by lane. 3 Proactive message: the cheapest lever; it targets the 62% bad-review rate of late orders while logistics is fixed. 4 Audit: ~1,100 orders are 'delivered on time' in the system while the customer says nothing arrived. 5-6 keep the fix visible and size the other complaint themes.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "color": "#1A202C"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The what-if: move the slider to assume a share of late orders had arrived on time; those orders take the on-time average score. Filter to a region or state to see where the gain concentrates.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#718096"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
